Error: `#[defensive]` marks no branch here
    ╭─[ src/main.inset:16:9 ]
    │
 16 │         #[defensive("the total is always there")]
    │         ────────────────────┬────────────────────  
    │                             ╰────────────────────── this statement is not a branch, and has no `?`
    │ 
    │ Help: put it on the first line of the `if`, `else` or `let ... else` block that no requirement can reach, on a `match` arm, or on a statement whose `?` no requirement can make fail
────╯
Error: `#[defensive]` cannot go inside a closure
    ╭─[ src/main.inset:19:13 ]
    │
 19 │             #[defensive("never zero")]
    │             ─────────────┬────────────  
    │                          ╰────────────── coverage does not count the branches of a closure
    │ 
    │ Help: mark the step that calls the closure instead, if it has a `?`
────╯
Error: a whole function cannot be marked defensive
    ╭─[ src/main.inset:30:5 ]
    │
 30 │     #[defensive("nothing adds")]
    │     ──────────────┬─────────────  
    │                   ╰─────────────── this would excuse every branch in the function
    │ 
    │ Help: mark each branch no requirement can reach: a `match` arm, a `failure` arm, the first line of an `if`, `else` or `let ... else` block, or a statement with `?`. Code no requirement can reach at all is unused, and should be deleted
────╯
